#    still pure background. The kept rectangle is the minimal bbox covering all
#    non-background output pixels: frame walls, inner 2x2 blocks, and every beam cell.
#    Example trace:
#    - Base task: a 20x20 input with one frame near the center and one NE beam that
#      reaches the top edge. Output stays 20x20 with large empty margins elsewhere.
#    - D12 variant: the same 20x20 beam overlay is first constructed, then cropped to
#      the bbox of all non-bg cells; if only the top edge is touched, the crop may keep
#      row 0 but still remove unused left/right/bottom margins.
#    - Difference: the beam logic is unchanged; only the final presentation is reduced
