#    - Any bbox-based crop must use the solved output, not the input. Cropping the input
#      first would delete empty runway cells that are needed for the beam simulation.
#
# 4) Placement legality:
#    Frames are still placed with the original non-overlap and in-bounds rules. The
#    generator additionally checks the solved overlay bbox and only keeps instances whose
#    crop is non-trivial, so the returned input is guaranteed solvable by the new main().
